INT. APIARY CONVENTION - HONEY TASTING TENT - DAY

White canvas. Folding tables laid with jars of every color from straw to tar. Hundreds of beekeepers murmur. A glass observation hive hums beside the podium.

DETECTIVE INSPECTOR INGRID LARK (40s, plain suit, notebook) walks the aisle. She stops at a stall where HORTENSE ABERNATHY (60s, honey sommelier, white gloves) arranges jars.

LARK
Mrs. Abernathy. About Alistair Penhallow.

HORTENSE
Terrible business.

LARK
He died at this table.

HORTENSE
He tasted the buckwheat and went blue.

LARK
You handed him the spoon.

HORTENSE
I handed everyone a spoon.

A MAN IN A BEEKEEPER'S VEIL (50s, tall, gloves) drifts behind Hortense, studying the observation hive. Lark glances at him.

LARK
Sir. Your name?

MAN IN VEIL
Ask the queen.

LARK
I'll ask you.

The man lifts his veil. He is KONSTANTIN GRIGORIEV (50s, weathered, one blue eye, one brown).

KONSTANTIN
Grigoriev. I sold Alistair his bees.

LARK
Then you know what killed him.

KONSTANTIN
Oleander nectar. A swarm that fed on it by the river.

HORTENSE
(sharp)
That's impossible. Those hives were mine.

KONSTANTIN
Were they?

A CLERK, FRANCISCO "PACO" LEMUS (20s, convention lanyard), hurries in carrying a ledger.

PACO
Inspector! The registry. Hive twelve was transferred last Thursday.

LARK
To whom?

PACO
(quietly)
Mrs. Abernathy.

Hortense sets down a jar. The room does not go silent, but the nearest ring of beekeepers does. She peels off her glove, finger by finger.

HORTENSE
Alistair planned to expose me. The adulterated honey. The syrup.

LARK
So you poisoned him.

HORTENSE
So I fed him his own greed.

DR. ISOLDE VANCE (30s, lab coat under a rain jacket, evidence bag in hand) pushes through the crowd and holds up the bag. A single dead bee lies inside.

ISOLDE
Oleander residue. Confirmed. In the spoon.

Lark closes her notebook. Behind them, the observation hive hums louder, and something in the glass catches the light: the queen, laying, indifferent.
